{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454829-what-s-your-favourite-blood-magic-path-s","id":1454829,"title":"What's your favourite blood magic path(s)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-13T08:37:29-07:00","id":1454829,"title":"What's your favourite blood magic path(s)?","content":"I love Necromancy in general on account of being an extremely macabre weirdo, but I think the Ash Path is my favourite. Extremely niche and never comes up, but I do so love the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:43:48-07:00","id":1454839,"title":"","content":"The Nightshade Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T10:55:20-07:00","id":1454844,"title":"","content":"Weather Control, easily, since it duplicates the classic Dracula ability to control the weather, and I am a sucker for anything that resembles classic movie/novel powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T12:59:55-07:00","id":1454850,"title":"","content":"Probably Spirit Manipulation and Ash Path, essentially because they provide access to portions of the WoD normally unavailable to Kindred. I also really like the Koldunic Way of Spirit, but it needs some reinterpretation or home-brewing to make it more balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T16:15:14-07:00","id":1454853,"title":"","content":"Can't really go wrong with Technomancy. I also really like Spirit Manipulation for letting the caster create fetishes, so its a good excuse to go delving through some of my WtA books. And then Path of Conjuring also gets a nod. Being able to pull literally anything out of your ass is always useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T08:32:32-07:00","id":1454887,"title":"","content":"Movement of the Mind for me, hands down. Not as flashy as some, but very versatile.<br /> <br /> Second place would be a tie between Soul of the Serpent and Path of Mercury,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T10:27:57-07:00","id":1454892,"title":"","content":"Oh what a question.<br /> Spirit thaumaturgy is something to build a really interesting character around.<br /> I like Technomancy in theory, but on paper it sucks.<br /> Movement of the Mind, Lure of Flames and Conjuring are awesome but kinda need houserules to function good.<br /> Corruption is glorious.<br /> Mercury is too strong. But it's awesome. I reserve it for Tremere lords and higher or other high-level masters. Use it well and it can make for a great villain.<br /> Path of Pleasure is dope (perhaps literally)<br /> <br /> I could be here all day. Worst path is Mars, which really needs improvments because it's writen as useful but it's mechanically a ditch. I hold to the idea that there's actually tons of useless/near useless paths that people can learn that aren't actually worth XP. If it exists, there's magic for it, but that doesn't mean it's useful.<br /> <br /> <br /> My fav necromancy path is Sephulcre. Ash and Virteous are temptations, but Sephulcre is THE necromancy path. I kinda hold the view that Thaumaturges should look down on necromancers. Necromancy is base and the practitioners are even wierder than thaumaturges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-15-2021, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T18:00:28-07:00","id":1454926,"title":"","content":"The path of Conjuring in the hands of a player or ST with IRL knowledge of chemistry, physics, or engineering more or less ends games. No house rules required. The same can be said for path of Technomancy if the people have a background in cyber security or other hacking experience.<br /> <br /> In a Tremere coterie, the conjuring specialist plays defence, the technomancy specialist goes on the offense, if anything survives long enough to figure out who their enemy actually is, some how survives the chantry to actually get to you..... 1. you screwed up, 2. thats what loyalist gargoyles and other arcane minions are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T19:46:42-07:00","id":1454930,"title":"","content":"I like Conjuration, but it can be downright busted. So I'll answer Path of Transmutation instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-21T19:25:16-07:00","id":1455338,"title":"","content":"I've always had a fondness for the Green Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T05:06:09-07:00","id":1455364,"title":"","content":"Nobody so far has mentioned my favorite two paths!<br /> <br /> The Focused Mind is great - for a Tremere that might end up in combat, it's pretty OP, and it has some useful non-combat effects as well.<br /> <br /> The Path of the Blood's Curse - it's extremely situational, but with this path a neonate can hunt a Methuselah and come out on top. Great path for a Sabbat thaumaturge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T11:23:45-07:00","id":1455867,"title":"","content":"I like Path of the Levinbolt a lot. It is so very useful in the modern age, able to disable or charge up technology as the Thaumathurgist sees fit. There is also the impression and intimidation factor - the users of this Path can certainly seem very stylish. The sheer power of this Path in regards to harming persons also speaks for itself. And the name sounds very nice.<br /> <br /> I also like the Path of the Focused Mind - the idea of a Vampire delving into the intricacies of her or his psyche through Blood Magic has a lot of appeal. To be able to think better is to be able to act better, in all the myriad ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-31-2021, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T14:43:07-07:00","id":1456037,"title":"","content":"I did not like paths and the old Thaumaturgy, there were at least 40 (by wikypedia). But years ago I played a Telyavevic Tremere and I liked the irony of having an spiritual path far more powerful than Necromancy, a very sign of unbalance in the former editions. The path was in Libellus Sanguinis 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T01:45:06-07:00","id":1456060,"title":"","content":"Oh those Paths were really cool- didn't one of them let you summon the spirits of dead warriors to attack your enemies? Way cooler than making some zombies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T02:47:52-07:00","id":1456064,"title":"","content":"I am gone go classic. Path of Blood. It is evocative, practical, diverse and logical. One of the very well balanced paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T06:26:06-07:00","id":1456069,"title":"","content":"If I'm going for a normal tremere, PoB/MotM.<br /> If I'm going to build a killer, path of Warding + Celerity makes you do at least 100+ agg levels of damage, even with low celerity, you only need two attacks or less.<br /> If I'm going to play to help my coterie, I'd probably make him with FM+PoB+Transmutation.<br /> If I want to make my friends and foes to live in a nightmare, I'd go with a Cappadocian, lots of controll, survavibility and insta kills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25853-moloch-the-gate-keeper","name":"Moloch The Gate Keeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25853_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T11:35:43-07:00","id":1456146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454829-what-s-your-favourite-blood-magic-path-s?p=1456060#post1456060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh those Paths were really cool- didn't one of them let you summon the spirits of dead warriors to attack your enemies? Way cooler than making some zombies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it let you: 1 See spirits, 2 Repel Spirits, 3 Command spirits, 4 Summon spirit warriors and 5 Enter the Underworld. In my opinion, far more powerful than the Necromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T09:01:59-07:00","id":1456188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454829-what-s-your-favourite-blood-magic-path-s?p=1455867#post1455867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Path of the Levinbolt a lot. It is so very useful in the modern age, able to disable or charge up technology as the Thaumathurgist sees fit. There is also the impression and intimidation factor - the users of this Path can certainly seem very stylish. The sheer power of this Path in regards to harming persons also speaks for itself. And the name sounds very nice.<br /> <br /> I also like the Path of the Focused Mind - the idea of a Vampire delving into the intricacies of her or his psyche through Blood Magic has a lot of appeal. To be able to think better is to be able to act better, in all the myriad ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also really like the concept of the Path of Focused Mind. But I have heard that the Path is kind of OP, and unlike the other ones I listed it doesn't actively expand your metaphysical awareness of the wider World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T04:26:10-07:00","id":1456224,"title":"","content":"In terms of usefulness path of blood, it's incredably utilitarian if you know what you're doing. For fun i really like the Mortis paths specifically the obscure Candaverous animation park from Dark ages-vampire since evil dead 3 is an awesome movie.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T10:36:14-07:00","id":1456308,"title":"","content":"If I had to say my favorite path, it would probably be the Path of Four Humors. There's several reasons why, but mainly the idea of a extremely powerful path lost to time is always interesting to me. For my 2nd and 3rd favorites, would probably got to Focused Mind and Spirit Manipulation, as it's rare for vampires to gain access to the Umbra, and Focused Mind is one of the most useful paths in the game.<br /> <br /> My 4th favorite path is path of Technomancy just due to one interesting idea that I had with it... so the 5th dot of technomancy says that you may project yourself into a electronic network... and use ANY technomancy power there. Now theoretically this means 2 things, a tremere can go to the digital web (although for a short time), and secondly could project themselves into the Technocratic Union's databases, and from there either, destroy them, or learn all of their secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T01:40:09-07:00","id":1456508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454829-what-s-your-favourite-blood-magic-path-s?p=1454892#post1454892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Technomancy in theory, but on paper it sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely disagree with that.<br /> \u25cf <b>Analyze.</b> A very situational opener for sure. Sometimes you need to operate accounting software or operate a forklift and in those situations, this will convince the GM to let you skip the roll. But infrequent use.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf <b>Burnout.</b> Break technology from 100m away? Fantastic! Win car chases by bricking cars. Break into buildings by bricking electronic locks. Fuck with lighting. Etc. Etc. Great power.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Encrypt/Decrypt.</b> The name and the fluff obfuscate the fact that this is a general-purpose ward. Each success is a +1 to the difficulty of operating a device. Ward doors. Ward elevators. Ward cars. Enjoy people rolling botches as they try to do the simplest tasks in their life.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Remote Access.</b> Pinnacle of the path. Could be an A-tier superpower for many superheroes.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Telecommute.</b> This is shittier Astral Projection, so don't get it if you also have enough xp to buy Auspex. Otherwise - you've got shitty Astral Projection at a discount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T03:00:23-07:00","id":1456511,"title":"","content":"I may have been thinking of something else. Yet, I still have some reservations when it comes to technomancy. <br /> -There are better (cheaper) rituals for powers 2 and i believe 3, and as you've said, 1 is very situational and 5 is &quot;shitty astral projection&quot; and it takes a long time to work your way up to the very desirable 4<br /> <br /> My main issue is that there's only one path and only so many rituals. You could easily make 3 or more &quot;tech&quot; paths along with goodness-knows how many rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}